   "rot": 240,
   "text": "THE COLDWELL\n\nThe river's source, under the glacier's lip."
  },
  {
   "wayside": false,
   "at": [
    800.42,
    117.99,
    -453.2
   ],
   "rot": 39.29,
   "tag": "thaw",
   "text": "THE ICE-FALLS\n\nYou cut a stick to come up, and leave it here for someone going down.\nThe rack is nearly empty. Everyone is up at the water."
  },
  {
   "wayside": false,
   "at": [
    800.42,
    117.99,
    -453.2
   ],
   "rot": 39.29,
   "tag": "rime",
   "text": "THE ICE-FALLS\n\nThe rack is full. There are more against the wall, and more on the ground.\nNobody has wanted one going down."
  },
  {
   "wayside": false,
   "at": [
    893.25,
    154.77,
    -472.71
   ],
   "rot": 3.18,
   "tag": "thaw",
   "text": "THE WELLHEAD STEPS\n\nYou can hear it from here.\nChildren are carried the last part, so they see it all at once."
  },
  {
   "wayside": false,
   "at": [
    893.25,
    154.77,
    -472.71
   ],
   "rot": 3.18,
   "tag": "rime",
   "text": "THE WELLHEAD STEPS\n\nThe snow on this bench has been sat in, at the left end only.\nSomething was put down at the right end, and picked up again."
  },
  {
   "wayside": false,
   "at": [
    901.7,
    157.15,
    -483.0
   ],
   "rot": 250,
   "tag": "thaw",
   "text": "THE WELLHEAD\n\nA thread on the post for each one going down the water this year.\nBlue, red and yellow. Eleven. It was a mild winter."
  },
  {
   "wayside": false,
   "at": [
    901.7,
    157.15,
    -483.0
   ],
   "rot": 250,
   "tag": "rime",
   "text": "THE WELLHEAD\n\nThe same eleven threads, white with frost.\nNobody came up to tie the next year's."
  }
 ],
